[ti:Day 22]

[00:00.00]align 例 It is too crazy to try to align the interests of management with those of shareholders. 试图 使管理层利益与股东利益相一致的做法非常荒 唐。
[00:10.45]collaborate 例 Knowledge sharing and information are often lost because of the inability to collaborate effectively either within the same department or across departments. 无论是在同 部门还是不同部门间，知识共享和信息经常由于 未能有效协作而出现缺失。
[00:30.28]spillover 例 The company has benefited much from the spillover of tourists. 这家公司从游客身上间接获 益很多。
[00:38.72]jackpot 例 The lottery jackpot has reached $150 million so far. 到现在为止，彩票头奖的累计奖金 已经达到1.5亿美元。
[00:45.69]entity 例 The authority has approved the agency is an independent commercial entity and the deal is also a purely commercial operation. 官 方音频已经证实，那家机构是一家独立的商业实 体，那次交易也纯属商业操作。
[01:00.83]blackmail 例 The man used her privacy to blackmail her to extort money. 那个男人利用她的隐私敲诈她 的钱财。
[01:08.60]congestion 例 That would reveal the currently hidden costs of congestion and increase the likelihood of airlines competing on service quality as well as on price. 这样就能揭露出目前 拥塞的隐性成本，并且增加航空公司在服务质量 和价格上竞争的可能性。
[01:26.83]conglomerate 例 The company is a broadly based conglomerate, with 16,000 employees in China. 该公司是一家分布广泛的综合集团企业， 在中国有1万6千名雇员。
[01:37.28]barometer 例 The global business barometer in The Economist is a survey to gauge trends in business confldence.《 经济学人》上的全球商业 晴雨表是一项测量商业信心趋势的调查。
[01:49.88]approximate 例 That product is a design that approximates perfection. 那件产品设计得近乎完美。
[01:57.78]eradicate 例 There's still a long way to go to eradicate the racial discrimination. 要消除种族歧视还有很 长的路要走。
[02:07.03]disseminate 例 The government has set up many platforms to disseminate environmental information. 政 府创建了很多平台来传播环境信息。
[02:18.28]collectable 例 Another popular trend is to buy historic gold coins with collectable nature. 另一个流行 趋势就是购买具有收藏性的历史金币。
[02:28.60]deface 例 The punishment for drivers who block or deface number plates on their vehicles will be doubled. 对于遮挡或者损坏车牌号的司机，将给 予双倍处罚。
[02:40.26]forum 例 At the action forum, we'd better establish task forces to implement action ideas on those themes that emerged. 在行动讨论会中， 我们最好建立起工作小组，以落实那些在专题讨 论中所产生的行动思路。
[02:53.53]cross-selling 例 Cross-selling can increase occupation probability of customers and improve the loyalty of customers. 利用交叉销售方法能扩大 客户占有率，提升客户忠诚度。
[03:07.19]cuddly 例 Over the years, these sweet and cuddly stuffed animals have been restructured to match the modernisation of toys. 过去几年，这 些可爱的、让人想要搂抱的填充玩具已被重新设 计以满足玩具的现代化。
[03:21.00]demotion 例 The demotion was unrelated to the academy's misbehaviour in the project. 此次降 级与该研究院在那个项目中的失误没有关系。
[03:30.51]harbour 例 The freighter was tied up at a small harbour. 货船停泊在一个小港口。
[03:36.54]cyberspace 例 Cyberspace presents challenges that are different from any we faced before. 网络空间 带来了我们以往未曾遇到的挑战。
[03:46.72]binding 例 Both sides have agreed the contract has no binding force. 双方都同意那份合同没有约束力。
[03:54.23]gangway 例 According to the dock regulations, you must fix up a safety net around the gangway just before discharging. 根据码头规定，你们必 须在卸货前先装好舷梯安全网。
[04:07.36]interior 例 He splashed out a lot of money on the interior decoration for the company. 他在公司 的内部装饰上花了很多钱。
[04:16.74]preconception 例 Did you have any preconceptions about the sort of people who did computing? 你对那些使 用计算机的人有什么先入之见吗？
[04:27.06]compensate 例 An unwritten contract here is that the winners shall use some of their wealth to compensate the losers. 这里有一项不成文的约 定，那就是赢家需要拿出他们部分的财富来补偿 失败者。
[04:40.06]impression 例 If you do better next time, then people will often forget their flrst impression of you. 如果 你下次做得更好些，那么人们通常会忘记对你的 第一印象。
[04:51.31]naught 例 If you don't stick with exercise, all the efforts you have made for slimming will come to naught. 如果不坚持运动，你为减肥作的所有 努力都将化为泡影。
[05:02.97]uncover 例 The report uncovered evidence of the company's illegal trade in wild animals. 那则报 道揭露了该公司进行野生动物非法贸易的证据。
[05:12.89]piracy 例 The government has adopted effective measures flghting the piracy of fllms. 政府已采 取有力措施打击电影盗版行为。
[05:22.53]backdate 例 The pay rise agreed in January this year is to be backdated to November last year. 今年元 月答应的提薪将追溯到去年11月份起算。
[05:32.72]plunge 例 The company plans to use the fund to boost innovation rather than plunge it into core business. 公司计划将这笔钱用作创新基 金，而不是投入到核心业务中去。
[05:44.24]knockdown 例 They sold the products to our company at a knockdown price. 他们把产品以最低价格卖给了 我们公司。
[05:52.15]whit 例 There is not a whit of innovation in the scheme. 这个方案丝毫没有创意。
[05:58.04]operate 例 The investigation shows that all of these factors operate against our advantage. 调查显 示，所有这些因素都对我们不利。
[06:08.36]enforce 例 The inspection of the dairy products should be enforced before they go to the supermarket. 一定要在奶制品进入超市前对其加 强检验力度。
[06:19.62]administer 例 America administered itself another dose of short-term austerity without addressing its long-term fiscal problems. 美国避开自身存在的 长期财政问题，实施了又一轮短期财政紧缩政 策。
[06:34.63]bilingual 例 During the Beijing Olympics, bilingual trafflc signs were erected around Olympic venues. 北 京奥运会期间，奥运场馆周围立起了双语交通标 志。
[06:46.28]deceleration 例 The deceleration in China's economy last year was partly because of a slowdown in property construction. 去年中国经济减速，部分 缘于房地产建设的放缓。
[06:59.95]accelerate 例 The institution is to accelerate its research in atomic power generation. 那家机构将加快原 子能发电的研究。
[07:09.87]preempt 例 Both parties need to work together to preempt the first strike. 双方需要通力合作以抢 占先机。
[07:18.04]affiliate 例 The International Development Association is afflliated with the World Bank. 国际发展协会 隶属于世界银行。
[07:28.36]charge 例 They do not charge at all for their services. 他们的服务概不收费。
[07:34.26]bedrock 例 The common interests of the companies are the bedrock of cooperation. 共同利益是公 司间合作的基础。
[07:43.23]combine 例 They have just established a newspaper combine. 他们刚刚建立了一家报纸联合企业。
[07:49.80]bicker 例 The two countries were always bickering over territory. 两国之间总为领土争执不断。
[07:57.17]insomnia 例 Insomnia even managed to ruin my work and daily life. 失眠甚至开始破坏我的工作和日常 生活。
[08:04.27]incompetent 例 Working for an incompetent boss can be bad for your development. 为一个不称职的老板 工作会对你的发展不利。
[08:13.12]containerisation 例 Containerisation techniques brought a revolution to goods transportation. 货柜运输技 术给货物运输带来了一场革新。
[08:24.24]banquet 例 They banqueted him royally when he became the director of the company. 当他就任 这家公司的经理时，他们为他举行了盛大的宴 会。
[08:33.22]calculate 例 The economic situation now is so complex that I can't calculate our flnancial status. 目前 的经济形势太过复杂，我难以估算出我们的财政 状况。
[08:44.20]enterprise 例 Our enterprise is listed as one of the world's Top 500 companies. 我们的企业位列世 界500强。
[08:52.91]guild 例 The guild achieved great success in China's reform of the market economic system. 行业协 会在中国市场经济体制改革中取得了很大的成 功。
[09:02.96]futures 例 The futures contracts are agreements to buy or sell at a certain price sometime in the future. 这些期货合约实际上是约定在将来某个时 候以特定价格买进或卖出的协议。
